          "kicker": "Squad call-up",
          "heading": "James McNabney earns first Ireland call-up after ACL recovery with Ulster",
          "body": "Ulster back row James McNabney, 23, was called into Andy Farrell's Ireland squad for the first time, learning of it while with Ulster in South Africa. He returned from an ACL injury in pre-season and said: \"I was delighted. It was a big moment for the family as well.\" Having given up horse riding at 16 to play rugby, he could make his debut in November's Nations Championship fixtures."
